>> title: Ramen Noodles
>> category: Noodles
>> tags: japanese, noodles, kansui, dough, make-ahead
>> counters: Ramen Shop
>> aka: ramen noodles, ramen noodle, rāmen, 拉麺, 中華麺, chukamen, chuka men, alkaline noodles, kansui noodles, fresh ramen noodles, noodle dough for ramen
>> pairs-with: tonkotsu-ramen, shoyu-ramen, shio-ramen, miso-ramen
>> servings: 4
>> time: 26 hr
>> slack: forgiving — at 38% hydration the dough stays a dry crumb, and anybody who adds water to fix that has made a different noodle

>> step: 38% hydration — the dough looks broken all the way through and that is correct.
38% hydration — the dough looks broken all the way through and that is correct.

>> step: dissolve the kansui and salt
Dissolve @kansui{5%g}(1 tsp powdered alkaline salts) and @fine sea salt{5%g}(1 tsp) in @water{190%g}(190 mL, cold) and stir until the liquid is clear.

>> step: rub to a dry crumb 5 min
Rub @&(~1)alkaline water{} into @bread flour{500%g} and @vital wheat gluten{15%g}(2 Tbs) with your fingertips ~knead{5%min}, until it is an even crumb the texture of damp sand with no dry flour left in the bowl.

>> step: press into a slab, rest 1 hr
Press @&(~1)crumb{} hard into a solid slab in a bag or under a rolling pin, then ~rest{1%hr}.

>> step: sheet to 1.5 mm, rest 30 min
Sheet @&(~1)rested dough{} through a #pasta roller{} in progressively thinner passes down to 1.5 mm, folding and re-rolling the first three passes, then ~rest{30%min} under a cloth.

>> step: cut, dust, rest 24 hr
Cut @&(~1)sheet{} into strands — 1.5 mm straight for tonkotsu, 2 mm wavy for shoyu, 3 mm for miso — toss them with @potato starch{2%Tbs}(20 g), nest them into 5-oz coils, and ~rest{24%hr} in the fridge.
